WEBVTT

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.580
Good morning, Amatsuyu!

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.120
Morning, Mom.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.040
You're chipper as usual early in the morning.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.960
After all, it's a magnificently merry Monday!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.250
I-I see.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.510
Oh, right!
You don't have school today, do you?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.470
Nope. The Flower Festival was on Saturday
and Sunday, so we get today off.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.180
But you don't need lunch, right?

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.600
Because you're going out with friends!

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.980
Yeah. Lunch is...

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.020
Wait. How did you know?

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.530
Your friend told me, of course!

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.530
My friend?

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.210
Good morning, Joro.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.960
O-Oh, no!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.270
<i>Today's luckiest person is you, Aquarius!</i>

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.140
EPISODE 07
I DISCOVER AN UNEXPECTED SIDE

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.730
<i>A change for the better may happen
in one of your relationships,</i>

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.820
<i>and you'll discover an unexpected side
to someone you're always with. Happy!</i>

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.690
Good for you, Amatsuyu!

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.240
<i>Well, see you later, everyone!</i>

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.240
You're number one!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.280
Yeah. By the way...

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.370
why are you in my living room?

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:04.780
It's a coincidence.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.870
You want to flesh that out?

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.960
While I was enjoying my daily stalking of you,

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.830
I ran into your mother by coincidence,
and she invited me here.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.670
That's not a coincidence!

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.880
Mom, why?

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.630
Sumireko was in front of the house,
so I invited her in.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.800
"Sumireko"?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:30.140
Before that, at a bookstore, I saw Sumireko reading
a book that one of my favorite movies is based on,

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.230
so I just started talking to her!

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.730
Right, Sumireko?

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.310
That's right, Laurier.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.320
Wh-What's "Laurier"?

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.780
Oh, Amatsuyu, what are you talking about?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.570
KEIKI KISARAGI (AGE ??)

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.950
If you take one character out of my full name,
it becomes "laurel," right?

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.320
LAURIER

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.910
KEIKI KISARAGI NICKNAME: LAURIER
FOREVER SEVENTEEN HEROINE (HOUSEWIFE)

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.450
Or, en francais, Laurier!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.910
<i>What's with these Japanese subtitles?</i>

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.460
Laurier, as sweet as cake!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.460
Because I'm going to make a get-well visit!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.540
You even came up with a tag line!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.840
Well, Sumireko, thank you
for keeping Amatsuyu company today.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.510
Not at all. I'm sure he'll take good care of me.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.720
ADMISSION TICKET

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.720
Let's have a good time today, Joro.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.930
S-Sure. Leave it to me.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.850
We'll leave after breakfast.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.640
Sounds good.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.610
AQUALAND

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.610
The time has finally come!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:29.490
Joro, you're just bursting with energy today!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.830
Well, sure! We're at the pool!

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.750
And you know what's at the pool.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.630
I'm a man, too, so I know just how you feel.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.010
Looks like the rest of them are here.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.340
We made it!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.800
Tell me! Am I cute?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.890
Yeah. Really cute.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.100
Yay!

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.520
H-Hi.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.980
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.110
Um, does this look strange?

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.490
No! It really suits you.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.700
I-I know, right? I'm quite the looker, right?

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.870
By the way, where's Pansy?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.540
Oh, she's...

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.290
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:25.800
U-Unusual for you to get the mood right.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.220
I know.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.970
But after all,
this is a totally original swimsuit episode.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:36.190
This very convenient day is born
from that passion. What else could I do?

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.940
I don't really know what you're talking about.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.900
All right! Let's have fun!

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.110
Come on, you guys!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.070
Yeah! Count me in!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.700
I'm right behind you.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:21.310
Damn it. If I'd only gone with scissors then.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.440
Cola for me and Sun-chan.
Orange juice for Himawari.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.740
President Cosmos and Pansy
wanted oolong tea, right?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.240
That voice.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.370
What are you doing here?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.580
Um, did I do something?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.420
<i>Who is she?</i>

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.380
Maybe you...

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.250
Yes?

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.050
Nothing!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.340
You look like a boy I know
who makes me sick! Sorry.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.850
It's an easy mistake.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.220
<i>Is it me, or is this girl emotionally disturbed?</i>

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:00.900
L-Listen. There's something I want to ask you.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.150
<i>It's like she can't leave me alone.</i>

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.820
<i>Where's the bench? The bench!</i>

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.530
<i>Not here, huh?</i>

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.860
What is it?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:15.370
- R-Really, it's about my friend.
- Okay.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:21.830
The thing is, she made a mistake
and was really mean to this one creepy boy.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.590
<i>Shouldn't that be in the present progressive?</i>

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.420
So what should she do in that situation?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:32.340
Obviously apologize, but she'd like
to do something besides that.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:35.600
This boy would probably forgive her
with an apology alone.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.560
She wouldn't need to do anything else.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.060
Don't give me some flip response!

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:41.770
Sorry!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:48.650
Whether he forgives her or not is low priority.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:53.280
He was treated shabbily because of me, so I
have to do something to make it up to him.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.240
Um, weren't we talking about your friend?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.160
I-It's about a friend
who's extremely close to me!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.420
<i>So close that it's actually you?</i>

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:09.760
If you were in that boy's position,
what would you want? Answer.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.720
If I were in that boy's position?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.220
Th-That's right.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.230
If it were me...

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.650
Y-Yeah?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.820
I would just want the apology.
I'd be satisfied with that.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.860
- I already told you, that's not—
- After all...

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.490
everyone makes mistakes.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.950
There's no need for her to be perfect.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.120
But what I did was awful.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:47.000
It's okay. If you have that pure feeling of wanting
to do something so much that it bothers you,

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.300
and then apologize sincerely,

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.550
I'm sure it'll come across to him.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.510
Even if they're on terrible terms right now?

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:59.470
If it's terrible, then whatever you do,
it can't get any worse, right?

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.180
Thank you.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.400
I see. It just has to be sincere.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.360
A sincere apology.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:14.900
B-By the by, I shouldn't give
a sincere apology with dyed hair, huh?

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.200
It probably depends
on the person's preferences.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.070
Tell me your preferences!

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:23.790
P-Personally, I like the neat
and clean feeling of black hair.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.960
Neat and clean! Creepy!

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.710
<i>Can this girl
just not help herself from hurting me?</i>

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.880
Here you go.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:39.260
Finally! They're probably tired of waiting.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.060
Here.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.560
Thank you. Not an apology, a thank-you.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.140
For answering my question.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.940
Th-Thank you.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.020
S-See you!

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.110
Acerola juice.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.750
It's so peaceful when that bench isn't around.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.580
Bench?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.250
- Joro, let's go—
- Joro, let's go—

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:10.460
Joro! Let's go on the water slide!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.210
Sure. Sounds good.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.420
Yay! Then let's go!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.220
Wait, Himawari.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:21.800
Sorry, but Joro already had other plans.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.470
That's right, Cosmos.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.680
- Joro is going to...
- Joro is going to...

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.020
- the hot spring with me.
- ride the dolphin with me.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.650
Joro is going on the water slide with me!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.780
- Hot spring.
- Dolphin.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:38.700
Water slide!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.530
Um, can't I do all of those things?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.580
I don't mind doing anything that's fun.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.660
Good point. Understood.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.790
You're right.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.120
You're smart, Joro!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.750
- Then, let's all—
- In other words,

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.630
the winner is whoever
Joro has the most fun with!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:55.590
Excuse me?

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:59.300
And as a reward,
Joro has to do whatever the winner says.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.010
Yeah! This should be fun!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.850
Then, we're all in!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.680
There's no way I'll lose.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.100
I'll do my best!

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.930
Um, I'm kind of caught in the middle—

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.440
It'll be all right, Joro.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.440
I take your feelings seriously.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.150
Only when it suits you!

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.190
Joro, I'm naturally going to win.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.780
You have nothing to worry about.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.110
All I have are worries!

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.820
Battle it out!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.830
Pansy! Cosmos! Himawari!

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.830
Hey! Sun-chan!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.540
It's a showdown, with Joro on the line!

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.420
Would you just listen to me?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.180
Let's splash!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.930
Why is this happening?

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.720
I'm up first!

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.350
Water slide! Water slide, Joro!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.440
Yeah, I know.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:59.820
<i>But still, this showdown...
"reward" aside, it's not a bad deal.</i>

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:05.950
<i>After all, three beautiful girls
are working hard to make me happy.</i>

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.290
Joro! Hurry up! Hurry up!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.540
Yeah, on my way!

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:13.580
Are you ready?

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.710
Yes!

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:15.750
Ready.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.590
Then, here you go.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.420
Let's splash!

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.850
This is fun!

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.970
Amazing!

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:31.430
It really is amazing!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:37.230
<i>Could this become
what I've heard about, a nip slip?</i>

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.610
- Let's splash!
- Let's splash!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:45.740
Where is it?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.080
Where's that nip slip?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:50.870
FREE GIFT

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.710
My watering can!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.830
That was a blast!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.210
Hey Joro, did you...

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:00.500
Oh, my gosh!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.300
Joro turned into a swimsuit!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.630
Wrong! Joro turned into his birthday suit!

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.890
- Oh, there you are!
- No.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.050
Hey!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:14.730
You surprised me!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.100
Wh-What?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.570
Another premonition of mine
that was right on the money.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.990
Sun-chan!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.450
Finally.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.700
Finally the time has come.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.080
It's my turn next!

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.960
<i>Oh. Boob alert.</i>

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.510
Joro, you ride in front. I'm in the back.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.630
Okay. I'll get on first.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.380
Oof!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.050
Now me.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.970
Boob alert. Boob alert.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.430
Look at the lovebirds!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.270
I bet they cuddle!

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:00.560
Kids are harmless.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.440
Let's not worry about anyone around us
and just have fun.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.620
<i>Meaning he wants to cuddle like lovebirds
while everyone is looking at us?</i>

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.240
President Cosmos? What's wrong?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.000
Certainly it's been my intention to date
someone with marriage in consideration, but...

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.170
<i>That's news to me.</i>

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:24.210
Uh, it's embarrassing being on this myself,
so if you could hurry it up.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:29.180
Hurry it up? Hurry up that plan?

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.720
You're so impatient!

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.060
Hey, wait a second!
A guy riding a dolphin by himself is...

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.730
Huh? Now that guy is riding
the pink dolphin by himself!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.360
That girl must have dumped him!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.110
President Cosmos!

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:47.860
Um, first, I'll go meet Joro's parents.
Or maybe he should come to our house first.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.110
She's in the middle of something.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.610
Damn it! Why does it always have to be me?

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.410
Pile on!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.790
In the nick of time, right?

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.540
Come on, Joro!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.290
Let's ride off into the sunset.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.300
Sun-chan!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:17.140
It's finally my turn.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.390
At this point, whatever.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.770
Come on, Joro.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.230
Hey, you don't have to drag me.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.080
This feels good.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.710
Tell me, Joro.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.630
What?

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.340
If you don't look at me,
making the effort won't have been worth it.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.470
I don't need to look!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.430
Thank you, Joro.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.100
Wh-What are you thanking me for?

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:05.060
This is the first time
I've have fun with so many friends.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.280
If you put it that way, then I'm grateful to you.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:16.490
Since you gave me that encouraging push,
I was able to make up with all of them.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.620
In fact, we may be even closer than before.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.960
So, um...

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.670
thank you, Pansy.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.590
You're welcome.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.060
Then, it seems you won't have to buy
a how-to book on making up

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:43.440
or pay a fortune teller to see
if making up with them is in the cards.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.020
You got that right!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.230
Hey, Pansy.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.400
Yes?

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.610
How did you know about that?

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.740
I didn't tell anyone about it.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.740
It was a coincidence.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.620
You want to flesh that out?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:04.500
I was enjoying my usual stalking of you
when I happened to see it.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.750
Again, you don't call that a coincidence!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:09.960
Honestly, what the hell?
You've just spoiled all of this!

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:10.750
But...

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.260
that's better than finding out
you hide dirty magazines

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:17.550
under the false bottom
of your desk drawer, isn't it?

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.970
How do you know about...

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:24.690
I accidentally ran across them
the last time Laurier invited me over.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.900
You couldn't accidentally...

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:29.610
And about the content...

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.570
Stop! Not another word!

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.610
Hey! Join us, you two!

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:45.830
I don't know what happened, but Joro's
falling apart here, so give him a break, Pansy.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.330
All right.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:51.090
I'll restrain myself for today.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.170
<i>Does she not exist,</i>

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:57.640
<i>a kind woman who'd do her best for me
without conditions?</i>

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.600
Sun-chan.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.070
All right, Joro!
Tell us the result of the showdown!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.280
Who did you have
the most fun with one-on-one?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.910
Although I don't really need to ask.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.660
I have confidence!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.580
It can't be anyone but me.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.370
Yeah. I made up my mind.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.420
The person I had the most fun with was...

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.210
Sun-chan!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.180
It was Sun-chan! Sun-chan!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:41.430
Nobody else even came close to Sun-chan!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:44.180
<i>- Joro.
- Please be gentle.</i>

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.890
So I'll do whatever Sun-chan orders me to!

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:49.730
Got it?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:56.320
Um, I feel like I should
apologize to everybody.

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:57.700
What is this?

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:58.900
We got shot down.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.110
Sun-chan, that's great!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.330
All right! Let's go home, best friend!

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.790
Let's do it, best friend!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.790
You're slow, best friend!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.500
I'm gonna leave you in my dust, best friend!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:19.720
<i>When I'm in a jam,
he races to my side and saves me.</i>

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:23.640
<i>I swear, nothing beats a high school boy!</i>

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.270
<i>Still...</i>

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.730
<i>why does stuff like this always happen to me?</i>

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:48.330
<i>This problem was settled safely, too,
so I guess I'll call it a win.</i>

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.040
Um...

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:55.670
you're surrounding me here.
Is there something I can do for you?

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.800
- I'm sorry!
- I'm sorry!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.340
I saw the newspaper.
I'm sorry for the things I said!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.760
I'm sorry I had the wrong idea!

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.600
I feel bad about that! I'll never do it again!

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.600
Oh. Don't worry about it.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.350
Thank you, Joro!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.060
It's just like I heard.
You really are a nice guy, Joro.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.440
Y-You heard?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:19.530
That's right. I heard.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:27.410
<i>What?</i>

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:31.910
<i>Who is this girl who looks so pure
and exactly my type?</i>

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.840
G-Good morning.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.210
Good morning.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:42.090
Wait! You're sitting in that chair!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.340
Don't tell me you're...

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.930
Yeah. That's Sasanqua.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.220
I said a lot of things I shouldn't have.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.810
Um, I'm sorry.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:56.020
<i>Today's luckiest person is you, Aquarius!</i>

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.820
<i>A change for the better
may happen in one of your relationships,</i>

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:03.320
<i>and you'll discover an unexpected side
to someone you're always with. Happy!</i>

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.700
This isn't the level of an unexpected side!

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:41.920
All right! Let's start homeroom.
Everyone, take your seats!

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:46.880
<i>Can a person change this much
in the space of a night?</i>

00:22:47.130 --> 00:22:50.930
We've got a new student in our class
from today. Her name is Yoki.

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:55.890
Go ahead, and introduce yourself, Yoki.
I want everyone to be good listeners. Huh?

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:02.980
I guess it's been a long time,
Amatsuyu Kisaragi.

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:05.070
It's been a long time?

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.740
Maybe you don't remember me?

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:12.490
That's terrible, when I clearly remember you.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.330
A kind woman who'd do her best for you
without conditions,

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:18.750
that's me.

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:20.080
So...

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.750
H-Hey! What are you...

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.260
From now on, I'll do everything I can for you
with all my heart,

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:34.430
so please be kind.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
EPISODE 08
BEFORE I KNEW IT,
MY TRAGEDY HAD ALREADY BEGUN

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.190
Before I Knew it,
My Tragedy Had Already Begun
